    "findings": [
      "18m6: projected Forward and Deferred blocks are separated by three condition bars for materials/lights, transparency, and bandwidth/device. Opposing arrows grow and the coexistence note avoids a universal winner.",
      "19-1: a projected camera/surface/wall/light arrangement distinguishes shadows, reflection and GI. The traced path grows through the arrangement; Cyberpunk RT Overdrive April 2023 patch 1.62 is labelled a technology preview.",
      "19-2: camera to first surface to BSDF direction to next intersection is shown with successive path segments and orange hits. Contribution is accumulated from sampled directions; the note does not claim all paths are evaluated.",
      "19-3: a projected surface emits several direction arrows, whose length and selected orange subset change across the stages. f(direction)/p(direction) and probability-density correction remain visible, with a poor-distribution variance caveat.",
      "All 44 samples on 11 boards have been directly read, including the last 12 samples after the saved progress. Black clean source views contain no burned narration captions; full moving and final composed pixels remain pending."
